## Rank / permission system (LOCKED)

Canonical: `RankBadgeService`, dyes (`CelestialDye` / `CitrusDye` / `RainbowDye`), Dev Menu Ranks, `player-ranks.yml` extras.

- **OP ≠ Admin / any Aetherion rank.** OP never auto-grants ranks or LuckPerms cosmetic ranks.
- **Admin = Robb UUID only** (`RankBadgeService.ROBB` / IGN A3therion). Never grant Admin from OP, LP, permissions, or name alone.
- **Rank assignment:** only Dev Menu Ranks. Players cannot self-assign or assign others. LP does not control Aetherion ranks.
- **Persistence:** `player-ranks.yml` is authoritative across restarts/reloads/OP/LP changes.
- **TAB:** keep level-colored titles; special rank BEFORE level rank; special ranks on right-side TAB where designed.
- **Special ranks (LOCKED with colors/effects):** Admin, MVP++ (static gold/red), Monkey (`CelestialDye` #B2FFFF), Citrus (`CitrusDye`). Do not flatten to plain text.

### Wipes vs ranks (GOLDEN — never break)

Special ranks and level ranks are **independent**.

- **Special ranks / `player-ranks.yml` extras (Admin, MVP++, Monkey, Citrus, …):** NEVER touched by any wipe, progress reset, storage wipe, quest wipe, or “full reset”. Not even for Robb/A3therion. Change **only** when Robbi does it himself or gives an **explicit** order to change that special rank.
- **Aetherion level rank (level-colored TAB title):** follows level/XP. A level wipe / XP wipe correctly resets it. That is expected and separate from special ranks.
- Wipe scripts must **hard-exclude** `player-ranks.yml` (and any special-rank store). Stripping UUID keys from that file is forbidden.

Do not touch Admin identity, OP/rank separation, Dev Menu rank UI, rank persistence, TAB rank display, or special-rank dyes unless Robbi explicitly requests that change.

